      "rationale": "The three reported failing checks ('pprint', 'token repr', 'single quotes') all stem from Token._get_repr_name picking str(ttype).split('.')[-2] instead of [-1]: this makes repr()/pprint report the parent token type (Keyword, Number, String) instead of the documented/intended leaf subtype (DML, Integer, Single), exactly matching the reported diff (\"...Keyword... Number...\" vs expected \"...DML...Integer...\"). The expected strings are derived directly from sqlparse's own token hierarchy in tokens.py (Keyword.DML, Number.Integer, String.Single) and from the KEYWORDS_COMMON/SQL_REGEX mappings that assign SELECT to Keyword.DML and quoted strings to String.Single, not from the current buggy output.",
